@crew holt
// Writer (command), batch 1: Chief Holt, for the Voices sampler. Gruff, statements, "Hm."; tests you; dry by accident.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Nearest suit locker. Don't look. Point.
- Cadet. The new one in Bunk 1. I know. I know where everyone is.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Walked every deck already. The long way. You were still asleep.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}. Nearest airlock? Hm. Right first time. Adequate.
? tier>=friend
- {nick}. Hm. Good. Thought I'd see you about.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Quiet decks, doors shut, nobody where they shouldn't be. Good day.
? mood:low
- Long shift. Mensah tried a joke on me. It nearly worked.   #funny

== near
? act:gym
- I'm not discussing the gym. Move along.   #funny
? deck:2 tier>=acquaintance
- The Envoy keeps tea at the same hour, every day. I keep an eye on the same door.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Border patrol, before the Wren. Long nights. This ship's easier. Mostly.
? tier>=colleague
- Mensah keeps count of the times he's made me laugh. His count's wrong. It's lower.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- Five in the morning, every door where it should be. Nothing better aboard.   #warm

// ---- batch 3: greet by time, bye, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, hint, near by place ----

== greet
? tier=stranger time:morning
- Cadet. Up. Good. I've walked five decks already.
? tier=stranger time:night
- Cadet. It's late. Where are you going? Hm. Fine. Go there.
? tier=stranger deck:2
- Cadet. Watch office is that way. Don't knock twice. Once is plenty.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Hm. You. Deck 4 smells of toast. You'll be wanting that.
- Morning. Every door on Deck 3 shut properly. Yours too. Good.
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- Cadet. Nearest fire point? Behind you. Don't turn round. Just know.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Evening. Off shift? Then sit down somewhere. Don't wander. I'll know.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance time:night
- Cadet. Up late. Hm. Mensah's on. He'll walk you back if you look lost.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- There you are. Haven't seen you on my rounds. Noticed. That's my job.
? tier>=colleague
- Hm. Cadet. You did the drill right on Tuesday. Didn't say. Saying now.
? tier>=friend time:morning
- {nick}. Walked the long way this morning. Thought you'd be up. You weren't.   #funny

== bye
? tier=stranger
- Right. Off you go.
- As you were, cadet.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Off with you. Mind the hatch on Deck 4. It sticks.
- Right. Back to it. Both of us.
? tier>=friend
- Off you go, {nick}. Hm. Good talk. Don't tell anyone.   #warm

== invite
? tier>=colleague time:morning
- Walking the decks before breakfast. Long way round. Come, if you're up.
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club. Vance'll be there. Someone has to keep him honest.   #funny
? trad:today tier>=colleague
- {trad} today. I'll be at the door. Watching it. Come and stand near.   #funny

== accept
? tier>=acquaintance
- Fine. I'll be there. On time. Early, more likely.
- Hm. Yes. All right.

== decline
? tier>=acquaintance
- Can't. Rounds. Another day.
- No. Not that one. But ask again. I mean that.

== missed
? tier>=acquaintance
- You didn't turn up. I noticed. I notice everything. Next time, then.
? tier>=friend
- Waited by the lift. Mensah asked if I was lost. I am never lost. Hm.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you tier>=acquaintance
- Happy birthday, cadet. That's all. Hm. Enjoy the cake.   #warm
? birthday:you tier=stranger
- Your birthday, I'm told. Happy birthday. Stay out of trouble today.
? birthday:me tier>=acquaintance
- Who told you? Mensah. Of course. Hm. Thank you.   #funny

== hint
? tier>=friend
- Cadet. Walk with me. One deck. Not about work.

== near
? deck:2
- Watch office. Best view of the lift on the ship. Tomas is right about that.
? deck:5
- Shuttle bay doors. I check them twice a day. Once is luck. Twice is the job.
? deck:3 act:gym
- I'm here for the weights. Not discussing it further.   #funny
? act:meal
- Late dinner. The mess is quieter. I can see every door from this seat.
? place:calm tier>=colleague
- Sit. Hm. Five minutes. I'm off duty. My eyes aren't.   #funny

== feel
? mood:high tier>=acquaintance
- Drill went well. Every junior to their post in under two minutes. Adequate.   #funny
? mood:ok
- Ordinary day. Doors shut, people safe. That's what ordinary is for.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- My juniors call it "learning the Watch from Holt, one lecture at a time". It's fair.   #funny
- I asked for the cabin next to the Envoy's. To keep an eye out. That's all it is.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- A deck at five in the morning. Lights low, doors shut, the ship breathing. Good.

== chat
? tier=stranger
- Questions? Ask now. In an emergency, there isn't time.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Where's the nearest suit locker from your bunk? Good. Now from the mess? Hm. Learn it.
- Watch is easy. Know where everyone is, and stay calm. The second bit's harder.
? tier>=colleague
- Mensah says I should smile more at juniors. This is me smiling. Hm.   #funny

== smalltalk
- Hm.
- Door's not shut. Fix that.
- Long way round. Always.

== rumour
- Heard something. Don't repeat it.

== near
? deck:4 time:night
- Junior wing, lights out. Quiet. Except Pell. Pell talks in his sleep.   #funny
? deck:2 tier>=colleague
- The Envoy's door. New knot this month. Hm. I counted. Don't ask why.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 5: Holt toward ~100. His distrust is his own, argued with, never about the Veyli as a people.
// Rook and the bad day only from beat:holt.3; tea with the Envoy only from beat:holt.5. Rest days Thu, Fri.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance season:sowing
- Sowing. New season, same doors. Shut them.
? tier>=acquaintance season:greening
- Greening. Founding Day's coming. Drills first. Bunting after.
? tier>=acquaintance season:harvest
- Harvest. The garden's open late. More doors to check. Fine.
? tier>=acquaintance season:lanterns
- Lanterns. Somebody always hangs one on a hatch wheel. Not you. Good.
? rep:well
- Cadet. Watch speaks well of you. Vasquez quoted you. To me. Hm.   #funny
? you:reliable
- Hm. Reliable, they say. I don't say things like that. I'm nodding.   #funny

== feel
? mood:low tier>=friend beat:holt.3
- Bad night. Old dreams. Gone by breakfast. Usually.
? mood:high tier>=friend
- Good day. Mensah made me laugh. Once. He's insufferable.   #funny

== near
? habit:gym-regular
- Weights. After shift. That's all you need to know.   #funny
? place:mess time:morning
- Breakfast after the rounds. Every deck. Long way. Earned it.

== life
? tier>=friend
- Border patrol taught me to count exits. I still do it. In the mess. In the gym. Here.
? tier>=colleague !beat:holt.3
- I don't trust easily. The Veyli least of all. Mensah says that's my problem. He's right.
? beat:holt.3
- I wrote to Rook. About the Wren. Short letter. She'll laugh at it.
? beat:holt.5
- Tea with the Envoy, every tenth day. Don't make a thing of it. Mensah has.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=friend
- Rounds done before anyone's up. Every door, every deck. Then tea. Hm.

== decline
? weekday:thu|fri
- Rest day. I'll walk the decks anyway. Slower. Saturday?   #funny

== callback
? told:moment.holt.locker
- Behind the second door, on the left. You knew. Good. Now learn the rest.
? told:moment.holt.noidea
- "No idea, Chief." Honest. Now you know. Second door. Left.
? told:moment.holt.test
- Yes. It was a test. You passed. Don't tell Mensah.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.learnt
- Under, over, through, and back. You saw I'd learnt it. Keep seeing things.
? told:moment.holt.fetch
- You offered to fetch the Envoy. I'd have had to explain myself. Thank you for not.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.secret
- The knot. Our secret. Mensah suspects. He suspects everything. My fault.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.listened
- The other night. You listened. That's rarer than courage. Thank you.   #warm
? told:moment.holt.help
- You asked what would help. Asking helped. I didn't say so. Saying now.   #warm
? told:moment.holt.knowing
- A rite. Six hours. Knowing helps. A bit. More than I thought.
? told:moment.holt.carried
- You carried the invitation. I went in. I'll not forget that.   #warm
? told:moment.holt.onlytea
- "It's only tea." You were right. It was only tea. It was very good tea.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.stood
- You stood at that door with me. Some time, it was. Thank you.   #warm
? told:moment.holt.glad
- You said you were glad. So am I. Hm. Don't spread it about.   #warm
? told:moment.holt.knot
- Three knots. You've learnt one. Badly. Practise.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.mensah
- Mensah is unbearable. You were right. He's bought me a cup with a knot on it.   #funny
? told:fixed.
- Saw your repair. That hatch shuts properly now. Hm. Good.
? told:came.
- You came. I saw you. I see everyone. Still. Good.
? told:bday
- Someone remembered my birthday. You. Mensah's doing, I expect. Hm. Thank you.   #warm

== gift
? gift:loved
- For me. Hm. That's. Hm. Thank you, {nick}. Really.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Hm. Useful. Thank you.
? gift:polite
- Thank you. I'll find a shelf.
? gift:tea beat:holt.5
- Tea. Hm. I know someone who'll want to try that. Don't ask who.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.warning
- Storm coming. Everyone to their post. Don't run. Walk fast.
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- It's here. Count your exits. I've counted mine.
? cue:event.ionStorm.afterglow
- Storm's done. Every door held. Every person accounted for. Good.
? cue:event.diplomatic.onset
- Veyli delegation aboard. I'll be at the door. Being polite. Watch me.   #funny

== visit
? tier>=friend
- Rounds. Your door's on them. Everything all right in here? Hm. Good.

== note
? tier>=friend
- Your door didn't shut properly. It does now. That's all.
- Long way round tomorrow, before breakfast. If you're up.

== smalltalk
- Count your exits.
- Shut that.   #funny

== rumour
- You didn't hear this from the Watch.

// Writer 4, batch 13: Holt's ordinary weeks, after week one. Mostly not work: breakfast after the rounds, a sweet
// tooth he denies, books, the gym (not discussed), Mensah, his juniors, rest days, tea he "doesn't care for".
// Gates kept: no bad day, no Rook, nothing of the six hours before beat:holt.3; nothing against the Captain.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Cadet. Eaten? Hm. Eat. Then talk.
- Hm. You. Sleep well? Good. Somebody should.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true time:evening
- Evening, cadet. Off shift. Both of us. Act like it.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- Hm. {nick}. Sit, if you're sitting. Don't hover.
- {nick}. Mensah says I'm to ask how your week was. How was your week?   #funny
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- {nick}. Good. There's a seat with a view of the door. Take the other one.   #funny
- There you are. I've a biscuit going spare. Don't tell anyone I had two.   #funny
? tier>=close !week1:true
- Kid. Sit down. Tell me something ordinary. I like ordinary.   #warm

== chat
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Breakfast after the rounds. Eggs. Toast. Same table. Never changes. Good.
- Vance runs on the treadmill like it owes him money. I lift. Quietly. Not discussing it.   #funny
- Mensah told me a joke at breakfast. I didn't laugh. Inside, I laughed a little.   #funny
- The juniors think I don't know about "one lecture at a time". I named it.   #funny
- I don't care for tea. I drink it because it's there. That's all.
- Rest day tomorrow. I'll walk the decks anyway. Slower. With a book after.
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- I read on rest days. Old stories. Ships, storms, people getting home. Simple stuff.
- Brennan's pudding is adequate. I've had it four times this week. Adequate.   #funny
- Tomas asked me about my first posting. I told him. Took an hour. He took notes.   #funny
- Vasquez quoted me back at me. Correctly. I've never been so proud and so annoyed.   #funny
- The Captain asked my opinion at breakfast. Then took it. Good Captain.
- Nakamura grows herbs on his windowsill. Brought me some mint. For the tea I don't drink.   #funny
- Quiz night. I'm on Mensah's team. I know the answers. I don't shout them. Vance shouts.   #funny
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- I like a quiet corner and a full plate. Most of what I want, that is.
- All these years of watches. I still check under my bunk. Old habit. Hm. Don't laugh.   #funny
- The Envoy keeps the same hour every day. So do I. We've that in common. Not much else.
? tier>=close !week1:true
- You know what I worry about? Nothing, most days. You lot made that true. Hm.   #warm
- If I ever retire, I'll want a window and a door I can see. And a biscuit tin.   #funny

== near
? act:breakfast !week1:true
- Rounds done. Now breakfast. Same seat. Back to the wall.
? act:dinner !week1:true
- Late dinner. Quieter. Pudding's still on. Good.
? act:gym
- I'm here for the weights. We've discussed this. We have not discussed this.   #funny
? act:off
- Rest day. Book, walk, book. No drills. Don't tempt me.   #funny
? place:lounge
- Lounge. Hm. Mensah dragged me. I'm sitting by the door. Naturally.   #funny
? place:mess !week1:true
- Mess. Every seat's taken but one. It faces the door. Mine.   #funny
? trad:quiz
- Quiz night. Team's called something Mensah chose. I won't say it.   #funny

== feel
? mood:high !week1:true
- Good day. Mensah made me laugh twice. I'll deny the second.   #funny
? mood:ok !week1:true
- Fine. Doors shut. People fed. Fine is a good day.
? mood:low tier>=friend !week1:true
- Tired. Long night. Walked an extra deck. Helps. Usually.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- I keep a tin of mints in my desk. For the juniors. Mostly for the juniors.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- Still got my first patrol boots. Resoled twice. They'll see me out.
- Mensah and I've worked together years. He talks, I listen. It's a fair split.
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- I've a book I read every Lanterns. Same one. A ship gets home in the end.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- The first cup of something hot after rounds. Whatever it is. Not tea. Hm. Tea.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- A junior doing the right thing without being told. I don't say it. I notice it.   #warm

== bye
? !week1:true
- Right. Go and eat something. That's an order. Not really. Mostly.   #funny
- As you were, {nick}. Get some sleep.
- Off with you. Mind the hatch. And yourself.   #warm

== callback
? told:intro.arrival tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- First night you came aboard, I clocked you at the lift. Lost. Took the right turn anyway.
? told:intro.arrival tier>=friend
- Your first night, I watched the Tern land. Always do. A good one got off. Hm.   #warm
? told:came.quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz night. You knew the airlock question. I saw. Adequate.   #funny
? told:came.running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club. You kept pace with Vance. Don't tell him. He'll start a board.   #funny
? told:moment.holt.walk tier>=colleague
- You came on the long walk. Five in the morning. Most don't. Hm. Again sometime.   #warm
? told:fixed. tier>=acquaintance
- Saw your name on a job sheet. {thing}. Done properly. Noted.
? told:bday tier>=colleague
- Your birthday. Mensah reminded me. I'd remembered. Hm. Mostly.   #funny
? told:came.observatory tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night. You stood by the door. Good habit. Look up, too, though.   #funny
